# Copy to config.local.ghostty (git ignores it) and keep what applies. Ghostty
# reads it after the whole of config, so a setting here wins over config's.
# Reload with Command+Shift+, (macOS) or Ctrl+Shift+, (Linux).

# Dracula PRO, a paid theme: theme-sync installs its variants into themes/
# and writes a block here, after the opening comment, that chooses one
# (Dracula-Pro at first). theme-sync and Neovim take the variant from the last
# `theme =` line: change it in the block, or name it after the block, then run
# theme-sync.
# theme = Dracula-Pro
# theme = Dracula-Alucard
# theme = Dracula-Blade
# theme = Dracula-Buffy
# theme = Dracula-Lincoln
# theme = Dracula-Morbius
# theme = Dracula-Van-Helsing

# Command+M opens Pi's model picker: send tmux a chord nothing else uses.
# This replaces Ghostty's Minimize action.
# keybind = super+m=text:\x1b[109;8u

# Herdr's sidebar characters (the herdr package). theme-sync generates the
# font from Dracula PRO into ~/Library/Fonts. Its name ends in a tag that
# changes with the drawings (faces/color_font.py): a running Ghostty does not
# read a changed font file again under a name it has loaded. After changing
# the sprites, put the new name here and in your copy, then reload: Herdr's
# own tests (not in git) fail until both name the current font.
# font-codepoint-map = U+100000-U+10007F=Herdr Sprites Pixel bb2d
